# Workers Jobs And Workflows

- Follow `AGENTS.md` and `MIGRATIONS.md`. Staging migrations are allowed; production SQL requires Logan's review and manual execution.
- All job-processing workers must call `isAutomationEnabled()` before claiming or processing queued `automation_runs`. Keep the gate fail-closed.
- Do not trigger, replay, deploy, or mutate production Trigger.dev runs.
- `workflows/permit-workflow.js` defines the 16-step durable permit workflow; keep step keys and run types backward-compatible unless the task explicitly changes workflow contracts.
- Legacy production processing still uses `automation_runs`; durable workflow paths bridge into legacy runs when enabled. Check both paths when changing behavior.
- Maintain idempotency, retry limits, checkpoint/resume behavior, and positive confirmation before irreversible actions.
- Do not mark permits, NOCs, recordings, or workflows complete solely because a click, enqueue, or API call succeeded.
- Use sanitized logging through existing worker/monitoring/audit helpers. Do not log credentials, tokens, signed URLs, PII dumps, or document contents.
- Safe validation usually includes `node --check` for changed worker/workflow files plus `npm run lint`; do not run production workers for validation.
